{"name":"Huntington Woods","hex":"#46554c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woods","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of wood"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dense collection of trees, usually one covering a relatively small area; usually smaller than a forest.","For chemical behavior purposes, trees in full leaf (coniferous or medium-dense deciduous forests)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woods"}],"entries":[{"title":"Huntington Woods, Michigan","blocks":[{"text":"Huntington Woods is a city in Oakland County in the U.S. state of Michigan. An inner-ring suburb of Detroit on the Woodward Corridor, Huntington Woods is located roughly 12 miles (19.3 km) northwest of downtown Detroit. As of the 2020 census, the city had a population of 6,388."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Huntington_Woods_City_Office.jpg/330px-Huntington_Woods_City_Office.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huntington_Woods%2C_Michigan","wikidata":"Q2466316"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"woods":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/22/En-us-woods.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/22/En-us-woods.ogg/En-us-woods.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 2","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_2.jpg/500px-The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_2.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Indian_grey_mongoose_(Urva_edwardsii)_mating_2.jpg","share":0.568125},{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 3","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/The_Indian